# ATLAS release payload manifest — the single source of truth for what ships
# inside a platform runtime bundle.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The payload used to be a hardcoded list duplicated in all three platform
# build scripts (build-windows-runtime.ps1, build-linux-runtime.sh,
# build-darwin-runtime.sh). Consistency was maintained by hand — the darwin
# script literally carried the comment "same source paths as
# build-windows-runtime.ps1". Anything omitted from the list silently never
# shipped, and no test asserted the three lists agreed. That is how
# services/cashflow, services/discord-bot, services/atlas-terminal and
# docs/imports/SKILL_INVENTORY.md ended up unreachable in release installs
# even though runtime code resolves paths into the bundle expecting them.
#
# FORMAT
# ------
#   <mode> <pathspec>
#
#   tracked   Copy only files `git ls-files -- <pathspec>` reports. This ships
#             SOURCE and nothing else: no node_modules, no .next, no cargo
#             target, no __pycache__. A pathspec that matches zero tracked
#             files is a hard build error, so renames cannot silently drop a
#             tree from the payload.
#   tree      Copy a path verbatim from the working tree. Reserved for build
#             OUTPUTS that are intentionally not in git (e.g. the prebuilt
#             cockpit bundle produced by CI earlier in the same build).
#
# Blank lines and lines beginning with `#` are ignored. Fields are separated by
# whitespace. Parsers exist for PowerShell, POSIX sh, and Node — keep the
# format dependency-free (no YAML/JSON) so no build host needs jq or a Python
# interpreter that is not yet bootstrapped at payload-copy time.
#
# SHIPPING DOCTRINE
# -----------------
# Ship source; build heavy artifacts on the user's machine at first use.
#
# A component is prebuilt in CI only when its build output is self-contained
# and needs no dependency tree at runtime. The React cockpit qualifies: it
# compiles to static files served by serve-dist.mjs, so `tree` entries carry
# the finished `dist`. Next.js applications do NOT qualify — `next start`
# requires node_modules present at runtime, and a cashflow bundle with
# node_modules and .next is ~1.3 GB against 1.4 MB of tracked source. Those
# components ship as `tracked` source and are provisioned on demand by
# atlas_runtime.provisioning, which builds into the persistent ATLAS_HOME
# rather than the immutable versions/<version>/ runtime directory that the
# updater deletes.

# --- Database schema -------------------------------------------------------
tracked infra/migrations

# --- Optional module framework --------------------------------------------
tracked modules

# --- Agent skills ---------------------------------------------------------
tracked skills/atlas

# Read at runtime by memory_router.py to route skill-inventory context.
tracked docs/imports/SKILL_INVENTORY.md

# --- Python runtime packages ----------------------------------------------
tracked packages/atlas-core/atlas_core
tracked services/agent-runtime/atlas_runtime
tracked services/agent-runtime/atlas_audit
tracked services/wiki-runtime/atlas_wiki

# --- Vendored Hermes foundation -------------------------------------------
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/acp_adapter
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/acp_registry
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/agent
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/assets
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/cron
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/gateway
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/hermes_cli
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/locales
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/optional-skills
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/plugins
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/providers
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/skills
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/tools
tracked foundation/atlas-hermes/tui_gateway
tracked :(glob)foundation/atlas-hermes/*.py

# --- Sidecar services shipped as source, provisioned on demand ------------
# cashflow_control.py:20 resolves <bundle>/services/cashflow.
tracked services/cashflow
# discord_control.py:27 resolves <bundle>/services/discord-bot.
tracked services/discord-bot
# cli/atlas_terminal.py resolve_terminal_dir() resolves
# <bundle>/services/atlas-terminal.
tracked services/atlas-terminal

# --- Go TUI module metadata (binary is copied separately by the builder) ---
tracked services/atlas-tui/go.mod

# --- Prebuilt cockpit (CI build output, not in git) -----------------------
tree services/web-ui-react/dist
tree services/web-ui-react/scripts/serve-dist.mjs
